{
  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) achieved 0.591 acc, a ~10.6 pp gain over the singleprofile baseline (config_001, 0.485), confirming that multiprofile + avgpool is the strongest design so far. Image-only is very weak (0.208), so the RNA modality is the primary driver. Uncertainty: We have not tested whether a transformer aggregation can further improve over avgpool for multiprofile RNA. This is a critical architectural decision that, if resolved, applies to all future multiprofile and multimodal configurations. Question tested: config_003 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer (holding rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000 fixed), giving a clean single-variable A/B comparison against config_002. Why this is the best next experiment: It directly isolates the aggregation question with minimal confounding, and the answer (transformer helps or not) will determine whether we need to spend budget testing transformer variants across encoders and modalities, or whether avgpool is sufficient. This maximizes information gain per experiment under the limited budget."
}

